# rcheevos is vendored upstream and ships CRLF in places. Without this, a
# checkout on a machine configured to normalise line endings rewrites all 116
# files and every diff drowns in 81k lines of nothing.
hasher/src/main/cpp/rcheevos/** -text

# Windows batch files are CRLF by definition; normalising them churns the diff.
*.bat -text

# A script has to reach every checkout with the line ends it was written with.
# Git for Windows turns core.autocrlf on unless told otherwise, and a checkout
# made that way hands bash a package.sh, a gradlew and the tests' scripts whose
# lines end in CR, which it does not run: the first `./package.sh` in Git Bash
# fails on a carriage return. The CI job on Windows gets round it by turning
# autocrlf off before it checks out, and a person does not know to.
#
# Above the two folders below on purpose: a later line wins, and what is under
# those folders is taken as it is, whole, whatever it is called.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# The hasher's library is committed with a manifest of SHA-256 sums of the
# files it was compiled from, and the check works the sums out again from the
# checkout. A checkout that rewrites line endings (core.autocrlf, which Git for
# Windows turns on) would hand it files that are not the ones committed, and it
# would say the library needs building again. Everything the library is made
# from is in these two folders, so both are taken as they are, whole: a header
# added beside the sources tomorrow is covered the day it is added. build.sh is
# in the first for a second reason: bash does not run a script whose lines end
# in CR.
shared/native/** -text
hasher/src/main/cpp/** -text

# A patch file writes a context line that is empty as one space. That is the
# format, and `git diff --check` is not to call it trailing whitespace.
hasher/src/main/cpp/rcheevos-patches/*.patch -whitespace

# The vendored folder is upstream's, byte for byte but for the patches, and
# upstream ends lines with spaces here and there. A space taken off to quiet
# `git diff --check` would be a change no patch names, so the check is told
# not to look there.
hasher/src/main/cpp/rcheevos/** -whitespace
